{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"targeted-spotless-newtnutria","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# DC parent sync is ONE-WAY: outbound writes the Epic Link, inbound never reads it\n\n## The asymmetry\n\nAfter Gerrit **1311** (ticket 39c1), `JiraDataCenterTransport.set_parent` writes a non-sub-task's\nparent to the instance-discovered \"Epic Link\" custom field. Nothing reads it back.\n\n`get_parent_map` (`transport.py:515-546`) — the ONLY inbound parent read — searches with\n`fields=\"parent\"` and extracts `fields.parent` alone:\n\n    for issue in self._paged_search(query, fields=\"parent\", rate_limit_retry=True):\n        parent = fields.get(\"parent\") if isinstance(fields, dict) else None\n        out[key] = parent.get(\"key\") if isinstance(parent, dict) else None\n\nRepo-wide, `Epic Link` / `_epic_link` appears ONLY in `transport.py`'s outbound path.\n\n**So a parent rebar sets on Data Center is invisible to rebar on the next inbound pass.** On DC,\ninbound can only ever see a SUB-TASK's parent — and [rebar:1a9f-50c0-e7a5-4fda] gives reason to doubt\neven that path takes effect.\n\n## Why this is the epic's signature class, again\n\n\"Cloud has the translation, DC never got its half\" — d067, 8d68, 751e, 2b16/88d9, 39c1. This is a\nfresh instance, created by the fix for the sixth one. Not a regression (nothing read the Epic Link\nbefore), and 1311 is not wrong — its scope was the outbound half, and the emit gate only ever emits\nan EPIC parent, so the Epic Link is the correct target. But the ROUND TRIP is open, and epic e369's\nheadline criterion is BIDIRECTIONAL reconcile.\n\n## The unproven risk that makes this more than cosmetic\n\nIf outbound writes a parent the next inbound pass cannot see, the differ may re-emit the SAME parent\nmutation every pass — the perpetual re-emission bug 8b25 was filed for (~230 steady-state\n`fields=['parent']` mutations on Cloud). **Explicitly NOT asserted here**: it depends on how the\noutbound differ decides a parent is already synced. The live cell that would show it is\n`test_a_repeat_pass_over_a_converged_pair_plans_nothing`, which is currently GREEN — so either the\nchurn does not occur or that cell does not cover this shape. Settle it before assuming either.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `get_parent_map` returns a non-sub-task's parent from the instance-discovered \"Epic Link\"\n      field, in addition to `fields.parent` for sub-tasks — field id discovered BY NAME, never\n      hardcoded, reusing the discovery+cache the outbound side already has rather than a second copy\n- [ ] the two shapes do not collide: a sub-task's `fields.parent` still wins where both exist, and a\n      test pins which takes precedence\n- [ ] the round trip closes: a parent WRITTEN by outbound is SEEN by the next inbound read, asserted\n      against a real DC instance on a harness run (run id recorded). A unit suite does NOT settle\n      this — changes 1276, 1288 and 1302 were all mutation-proven and all wrong live\n- [ ] idempotence is proven, not assumed: repeated passes over a converged epic-parent pair emit NO\n      further parent mutation — this is the churn risk above\n- [ ] `get_parent_map`'s degradation contract is preserved: a failure still logs a WARNING and\n      returns `{}` so the inbound pass falls back to parentless rather than aborting\n- [ ] `transport.py` stays under the 800-LOC cap (it is ~781 after 1311; the discovery helper\n      already exists, so this should reuse it rather than grow a parallel one)","id":"9bb9-56a3-e9c0-46e9","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"DC parent sync is one-way: outbound writes the Epic Link, inbound never reads it"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785794289175691001,"uuid":"39b56fb1-36ad-42c3-8cbb-0c3333be8b0f"}